{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna","id":1353497,"title":"Yama Kings and Maeljin Incarna","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-07T23:33:20-08:00","id":1353497,"title":"Yama Kings and Maeljin Incarna","content":"So in the Dragons on the East book it says that the Scarlet Queen is the Weaver, and the Ebon Dragon is the Wyrm (and the Tiger is the Wyld). With that in mind, and the fact that the Ebon Dragon had Yama King ministers, why can't the Yama Kings and the Maeljin Incarna travel to or invade each other's spirit realms (in I think The 1000 Hells it says the Yama Kings and Maeljin Incarna can send emissaries to and trade souls and such with each other, but can't actually go to or invade one another's realms.) In fact until the Great Leap Outward the Yama Kings had no direct influence outside the Middle Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Going with the assumption made in Dragons of the East about the Triat and being willing to step on the cosmic toes of the various games' creation myths, why do the Yama Kings have no direct power in the West, and the Maeljin Incarna no direct power in the Middle Kingdoms?<br /> <br /> Could it have something to do with the consensus and the beliefs of people? Based on something said in The 1000 Hells, could they be different masks/personalities/incarnations/mantles for the same things while being unaware of this fact?<br /> <br /> The thing I'm referencing in The 1000 Hells says &quot;While there is a constant exchange of flesh and other goods between Malfeas and Yomi, the primary reason that the Yama Kings and Malfeans aren't at each other's throats is that they have too much in common -- everything, in fact, except sphere of influence.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":".  To provide clarification. 12-08-2019, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T08:35:36-08:00","id":1353552,"title":"","content":"The metaphysic trinity entry from DotE isn't really something to be taken at face value, given how it's generally all over the place and draws lines between things that don't match up (somehow, Dragon is both Yin and Balance, for example). Secondly, nothing in Werewolf has to do with consensus; the Maeljin don't care about, and wouldn't be stopped by it. Only the presence of rival spirits of comparable or greater power keeps them in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T09:02:05-08:00","id":1353561,"title":"","content":"The manner in which the end of the Wraith game line sets up the cosmology of the Hunter game line is an exception, rather than the rule. The game lines largely have their own separate cosmologies. <br /> <br /> If something resembling the Werewolf Triat or claiming to believe in the Triat appears in your Kindred of the East game, it's a cool easter egg, but I'd recommend against worrying about how two cosmologies from what are really two separate game worlds can both be true at the same time if they don't seem easily compatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T09:57:04-08:00","id":1353573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1353561#post1353561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The manner in which the end of the Wraith game line sets up the cosmology of the Hunter game line is an exception, rather than the rule. The game lines largely have their own separate cosmologies. <br /> <br /> If something resembling the Werewolf Triat or claiming to believe in the Triat appears in your Kindred of the East game, it's a cool easter egg, but I'd recommend against worrying about how two cosmologies from what are really two separate game worlds can both be true at the same time if they don't seem easily compatible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragons of the East is a Mage The Ascension Book, so I\u2019m not quite following.<br /> <br /> That aside I\u2019m working out ways to connect the mythologies together (for a game I plan to run where it\u2019s appropriate), and have largely been successful so far (after digging through dozens upon dozens of books, forums and real world mythology wikis. The Yama Kings and Maeljin Incarna thing is a bit of a thorn so far though.<br /> <br /> I could hand wave it, but it\u2019s of interest and use to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 12-08-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T10:17:06-08:00","id":1353577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1353573#post1353573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dragons of the East is a Mage The Ascension Book, so I\u2019m not quite following.<br /> <br /> That aside I\u2019m working out ways to connect the mythologies together (for a game I plan to run where it\u2019s appropriate), and have largely been successful so far (after digging through dozens upon dozens of books, forums and real world mythology wikis. The Yama Kings and Maeljin Incarna thing is a bit of a thorn so far though.<br /> <br /> I could hand wave it, but it\u2019s of interest and use to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The key thing to note here is that unless you're really into Mage, it's probably better for your crossover to drop aspects of it or minimize its influence. It makes more assumptions about the world that other games can't run with than any other single WoD game, and you can't really plug them in to operate in parallel like with W:tA, where the Middle Umbral spiritual realms exist in concert with whatever else gets piled on, even if they're not easily accessible to others. This is important, because you can't plug Werewolf and Mage in and expect them to work; they make mutually exclusive claims about the cosmos, and operate in a strict binary, where choosing one means letting the other go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T11:13:23-08:00","id":1353587,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s true if you\u2019re taking them wholesale, but not if you approach it with the assumption that they aren\u2019t getting everything right, or that there\u2019s something going on like in Scion.<br /> <br /> With what I\u2019m doing I don't mind stepping on some cosmic mythology toes. I\u2019m looking for any known canon reasons or any reasonable assumptions/suggestions as to why the Yama Kings and Maeljin Incarna can\u2019t directly influence or invade each other\u2019s realms. I do hope I'm not coming off as being abrasive, which, if I am, I apologize for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 12-08-2019, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T12:42:25-08:00","id":1353606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1353587#post1353587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s true if you\u2019re taking them wholesale, but not if you approach it with the assumption that they aren\u2019t getting everything right, or that there\u2019s something going on like in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you assume that a given game is getting it wrong, that tends to injure its core play experience. They weren't really taken to be an ironic exploration of the material that they represent or use. They were also intentionally designed to fall apart in crossovers, so there's no absolute big picture even going on, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With what I\u2019m doing I don't mind stepping on some cosmic mythology toes. I\u2019m looking for any known canon reasons or any reasonable assumptions/suggestions as to why the Yama Kings and Maeljin Incarna can\u2019t directly influence or invade each other\u2019s realms. I do hope I'm not coming off as being abrasive, which, if I am, I apologize for. </div> </div> </div>The Yama Kings are squatting in a half-underworld half-middle umbra, so their domain just might not be extremely accessible. Others would lose fighting them on their turf, but they wouldn't fare particularly well if they tried venturing outward... except for Mikaboshi. Umbra Revised has The Wicked City adjoining part of the CyberRealm. That potential plot seed seems to have not made it into W20, though.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, for most of the life of W:tA, Malfeas was in the Deep Umbra rather than Near Umbra, so the Maeljin might have actually been more distant in some respects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T12:57:05-08:00","id":1353932,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was thinking that the Maeljin Incarnae originating from a home base out past the horizon might make any direct interaction with nearer umbral realms difficult if not impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T16:22:23-08:00","id":1353991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1353606#post1353606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you assume that a given game is getting it wrong, that tends to injure its core play experience. They weren't really taken to be an ironic exploration of the material that they represent or use. They were also intentionally designed to fall apart in crossovers, so there's no absolute big picture even going on, either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Yama Kings are squatting in a half-underworld half-middle umbra, so their domain just might not be extremely accessible. Others would lose fighting them on their turf, but they wouldn't fare particularly well if they tried venturing outward... except for Mikaboshi. Umbra Revised has The Wicked City adjoining part of the CyberRealm. That potential plot seed seems to have not made it into W20, though.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, for most of the life of W:tA, Malfeas was in the Deep Umbra rather than Near Umbra, so the Maeljin might have actually been more distant in some respects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you\u2019re saying, though I\u2019d say that all depends on the type of game you\u2019re running, so long as proper expectations are set with the players and they\u2019re good with playing in said game. Wouldn\u2019t want it to be a bait and switch, even unintentionally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:38:36-08:00","id":1354465,"title":"","content":"There's another reason they may have different domains, at least: in Wraith, souls are different in different continents. African wraiths have a four-part soul, for instance. So it's entirely possible that the Yama Kings only have influence over the P'o and that this influence doesn't extend to the Shadow. That would limit their influence to those regions where beings have the traditional Middle Kingdom soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T16:51:34-08:00","id":1354491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1354465#post1354465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's another reason they may have different domains, at least: in Wraith, souls are different in different continents. African wraiths have a four-part soul, for instance. So it's entirely possible that the Yama Kings only have influence over the P'o and that this influence doesn't extend to the Shadow. That would limit their influence to those regions where beings have the traditional Middle Kingdom soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complication: until the writing changes, the po basically is the same thing as a shadow. If it were truer to the real life lore regarding the hunpo, it'd be different, but that's not what we have. As to what differences this would entail...<br /> <br /> -The po is the seat of passions. Unlike wraiths with a psyche and shadow, there would be no division of passions - they would all be a part of the po, even if you were ashamed of them. There's even a neat list of which of the Daoist wuxing to which your passions would correspond, though that's perhaps more mechanics than might be comfortable. In any case, &quot;shadow passions&quot; simply wouldn't exist under this paradigm, if it were executed to be true to real life inspirations.<br /> <br /> -The hun is the seat of relationships. So, this is a stretch, but I would take that to mean that your Fetters would be wholly associated with your hun. Normally, it'd presumably focus on the relationships you have with others in society, like the ones outlined in Confucianism, but objects can probably fit in if we're trying to cram W:tO into other systems.<br /> <br /> A bit of a rambling tangent, but the takeaway is that there's a fair bit of work before we actually move away from the psyche and shadow in the DKoJ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T15:25:08-08:00","id":1354825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1354491#post1354491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Complication: until the writing changes, the po basically is the same thing as a shadow. If it were truer to the real life lore regarding the hunpo, it'd be different, but that's not what we have. As to what differences this would entail...<br /> <br /> -The po is the seat of passions. Unlike wraiths with a psyche and shadow, there would be no division of passions - they would all be a part of the po, even if you were ashamed of them. There's even a neat list of which of the Daoist wuxing to which your passions would correspond, though that's perhaps more mechanics than might be comfortable. In any case, &quot;shadow passions&quot; simply wouldn't exist under this paradigm, if it were executed to be true to real life inspirations.<br /> <br /> -The hun is the seat of relationships. So, this is a stretch, but I would take that to mean that your Fetters would be wholly associated with your hun. Normally, it'd presumably focus on the relationships you have with others in society, like the ones outlined in Confucianism, but objects can probably fit in if we're trying to cram W:tO into other systems.<br /> <br /> A bit of a rambling tangent, but the takeaway is that there's a fair bit of work before we actually move away from the psyche and shadow in the DKoJ.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think trying to fit real world concepts into this doesn't work but you're right that those concepts are more overtly different in RL terms. <br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is a mess of influences, so they don't map neatly. But Western Wraiths specifically can't learn the Arcanoi of the Dark Kingdom of Jade because of the explicit and implicit 'differences' in their souls.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Eidolon is superficially the Hun and the Shadow is the P'o in broad terms, but Wraith says that they're still somewhat different. Part of that is the attitude to each part of the soul, but metaphysically they're not identical either. (To be honest, a large part of this is exoticism and an attempt at mystery. We're frequently told how different everything is in Asia.)<br /> <br /> Another distinct possibility is that Yomi relies on reincarnation to some degree. Dhampyrs, for instance, are reincarnations of the children of the Wan Xian. It's possible that the Wan Kuei are reincarnations of the Wan Xian in a similar way, though this isn't likely to be in canon anyway. It might be that these souls are always destined to return to the same place in between lives. Therefore souls who haven't previously been bound to the Yama Kings might not be in their reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-14-2019, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T18:20:39-08:00","id":1354841,"title":"","content":"I kind of thought the Hun was more like a wraith\u2019s Eidolon, being that it\u2019s the higher self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T23:56:55-08:00","id":1354859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1354841#post1354841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of thought the Hun was more like a wraith\u2019s Eidolon, being that it\u2019s the higher self.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. It was late. The Hun is supposed to be the Eidolon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T17:35:34-08:00","id":1354944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1354841#post1354841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of thought the Hun was more like a wraith\u2019s Eidolon, being that it\u2019s the higher self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly enough one KotE book also correlates the hun/po to the WTA gnosis/rage system. It's intended for any effect that requires a rage or gnosis rolls to resist a wan kuei can use hun/po as appropriate, but taking it into account with Mage, sorcerer, and the hunter books, it kinda explains how just about All supernatural powers work.<br /> <br /> One of the ST vault books that acts as a companion/errata for sorcerer revised points at this(most likely accidental) correlation, and I've extrapolated form there.<br /> <br /> All (linear) supernaturals have 3 &quot;soul&quot; values that can store up to 30 &quot;magic&quot; points total, the values being Higher soul(gnosis/hun/eidolon/mana/glamour/avatar/balance/humanity/etc), Lower soul (rage/po/angst/etc), and Willpower(or being for spectres). For most supernaturals these values are either hidden or the supernatural is unable to use them for magic points for one reason or another.<br /> <br /> All supernaturals can also store external Tass/magic points(vitae in kindred, chi in wan kuei or shih) in their bodies up to a theoretically infinite amount, but usually limited to 10 points. The limitations on how this works is dependent on the method used to manipulate it and how good they are at using that ability. Kindred let the blood of caine in their bodies do all the work and are limited by the quality of the blood they first get(generation). Wan Kuei have to actually develop their skills and can thus increase their &quot;Capacity&quot; as they get better. Shih develop their skills like Wan kuei, but are stuck with their human limitations in how good they can get. Ghouls are surprising in that they can passively develop their &quot;Capacity&quot;(as they age, their vitae capacity increases without limit, but they're still limited on how they can Use that vitae).<br /> <br /> Magic Points themselves come in 2 flavors, yin and yang(or life and death, or active and passive, or etc). As stated in KotE, kindred+wraiths are examples of all Yin magic creatures and mummies+garou(and the wider fera and bete) are examples of all Yang magic users. depending on if used &quot;As Is&quot; for magic if the supernatural has the right corresponding personality traits(called &quot;Virtues&quot;) or filtered by one of the &quot;Soul Values&quot;, the user can change what magic they can use.<br /> <br /> Werewolves channel &quot;Yang&quot; magic through their Higher Soul to either change themselves in a lasting way or shape the natural world and channel it through their lower soul to actively ignore their body's natural limits or inflict destructive power(both through collecting individual &quot;Gifts&quot; of varying level). Mummies are similar, but channel &quot;yang&quot; magic exclusively through their Higher Soul to change the natural world(through individual &quot;Spells&quot; of varying level).<br /> <br /> Vampires are allowed to channel raw &quot;Yin&quot; by the curse of caine and can channel it to passively multiply the natural abilities of their bodies or into strict successions of powers called &quot;disciplines&quot;. Wraiths channel Yin magic by pushing it through force of will into strict successions of grouped powers called &quot;arcanoi&quot;. Yin magic of wraiths/vampires differ from the yang magic of bete/mummies in that they aren't collected individually, they're abilities that are painstakingly build upon themselves a clear line of succession. Also notably is the fact that yin magic doesn't allow a creature to overcome their body's natural limitations like a werewolf channeling yang through their Lower Soul(Rage), they allow both vampires/risen wraiths to Increase their bodies natural abilities and said increases last for much longer than the instant power brought by yang. Yin changes can possibly be made permanent as well(with fortitude/potence/celerity)<br /> <br /> Changelings are a bit weird, in that they channel exclusively through their Higher Soul(glamour) and can increase their power by channeling unfiltered Yang, but increasing their corresponding Tass virtues(banality and nightmare/imbalance) is actually a Bad thing. Yin Tass is also poisonous to them in general.<br /> <br /> Mages and Sorcerers sanitize their raw magic of any yin/yang affiliation and channel the bland remains through their Higher soul(mana/avatar). They are barely able to use it for much beyond making their unrelated magic(paths/spheres) easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 12-15-2019, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T03:27:47-08:00","id":1355156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1354944#post1354944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weirdly enough one KotE book also correlates the hun/po to the WTA gnosis/rage system. It's intended for any effect that requires a rage or gnosis rolls to resist a wan kuei can use hun/po as appropriate, but taking it into account with Mage, sorcerer, and the hunter books, it kinda explains how just about All supernatural powers work.<br /> <br /> One of the ST vault books that acts as a companion/errata for sorcerer revised points at this(most likely accidental) correlation, and I've extrapolated form there.<br /> <br /> All (linear) supernaturals have 3 &amp;quot;soul&amp;quot; values that can store up to 30 &amp;quot;magic&amp;quot; points total, the values being Higher soul(gnosis/hun/eidolon/mana/glamour/avatar/balance/humanity/etc), Lower soul (rage/po/angst/etc), and Willpower(or being for spectres). For most supernaturals these values are either hidden or the supernatural is unable to use them for magic points for one reason or another.<br /> <br /> All supernaturals can also store external Tass/magic points(vitae in kindred, chi in wan kuei or shih) in their bodies up to a theoretically infinite amount, but usually limited to 10 points. The limitations on how this works is dependent on the method used to manipulate it and how good they are at using that ability. Kindred let the blood of caine in their bodies do all the work and are limited by the quality of the blood they first get(generation). Wan Kuei have to actually develop their skills and can thus increase their &amp;quot;Capacity&amp;quot; as they get better. Shih develop their skills like Wan kuei, but are stuck with their human limitations in how good they can get. Ghouls are surprising in that they can passively develop their &amp;quot;Capacity&amp;quot;(as they age, their vitae capacity increases without limit, but they're still limited on how they can Use that vitae).<br /> <br /> Magic Points themselves come in 2 flavors, yin and yang(or life and death, or active and passive, or etc). As stated in KotE, kindred+wraiths are examples of all Yin magic creatures and mummies+garou(and the wider fera and bete) are examples of all Yang magic users. depending on if used &amp;quot;As Is&amp;quot; for magic if the supernatural has the right corresponding personality traits(called &amp;quot;Virtues&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> or filtered by one of the &amp;quot;Soul Values&amp;quot;, the user can change what magic they can use.<br /> <br /> Werewolves channel &amp;quot;Yang&amp;quot; magic through their Higher Soul to either change themselves in a lasting way or shape the natural world and channel it through their lower soul to actively ignore their body's natural limits or inflict destructive power(both through collecting individual &amp;quot;Gifts&amp;quot; of varying level). Mummies are similar, but channel &amp;quot;yang&amp;quot; magic exclusively through their Higher Soul to change the natural world(through individual &amp;quot;Spells&amp;quot; of varying level).<br /> <br /> Vampires are allowed to channel raw &amp;quot;Yin&amp;quot; by the curse of caine and can channel it to passively multiply the natural abilities of their bodies or into strict successions of powers called &amp;quot;disciplines&amp;quot;. Wraiths channel Yin magic by pushing it through force of will into strict successions of grouped powers called &amp;quot;arcanoi&amp;quot;. Yin magic of wraiths/vampires differ from the yang magic of bete/mummies in that they aren't collected individually, they're abilities that are painstakingly build upon themselves a clear line of succession. Also notably is the fact that yin magic doesn't allow a creature to overcome their body's natural limitations like a werewolf channeling yang through their Lower Soul(Rage), they allow both vampires/risen wraiths to Increase their bodies natural abilities and said increases last for much longer than the instant power brought by yang. Yin changes can possibly be made permanent as well(with fortitude/potence/celerity)<br /> <br /> Changelings are a bit weird, in that they channel exclusively through their Higher Soul(glamour) and can increase their power by channeling unfiltered Yang, but increasing their corresponding Tass virtues(banality and nightmare/imbalance) is actually a Bad thing. Yin Tass is also poisonous to them in general.<br /> <br /> Mages and Sorcerers sanitize their raw magic of any yin/yang affiliation and channel the bland remains through their Higher soul(mana/avatar). They are barely able to use it for much beyond making their unrelated magic(paths/spheres) easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above is true for crossover purposes, but it's also reductive from an IC perspective (except for the Wan Kuei, perhaps, who see everything through their lens). For example, in KotE's spirit rules, Rage is actually Yang and Gnosis is Yin. So it's not as simple as Rage always being P'o, because sometimes it's not.<br /> <br /> Likewise, mummies have however many soul 'parts' IC, which contradicts other gamelines. You could argue that the Yama Kings only *believe* they can claim Asian souls, which then makes it true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T10:59:57-08:00","id":1355214,"title":"","content":"Rage and Gnosis kind of even out when it comes to Daoist division of primary poles. Rage is furious and active like a forest fire, which is yang, but also wrapped up in anger, which is the negative side of Benevolence, or in other words, yin. Gnosis is calm and contemplative, thus fulfilling a &quot;soft, internal&quot; sort of power, but also the side of Garou and Fera that represents a &quot;higher&quot; spiritual core unbound by the material, which is yang. Most denizens of the WoD probably fall along these lines unless there would be a compelling reason otherwise, like having been split apart and re-bound in the manner of the Hungry Dead, or ghosts being given power from passions while dead, which is pretty heavily yin over yang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T15:52:17-08:00","id":1355283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1355156#post1355156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of the above is true for crossover purposes, but it's also reductive from an IC perspective (except for the Wan Kuei, perhaps, who see everything through their lens). For example, in KotE's spirit rules, Rage is actually Yang and Gnosis is Yin. So it's not as simple as Rage always being P'o, because sometimes it's not.<br /> <br /> Likewise, mummies have however many soul 'parts' IC, which contradicts other gamelines. You could argue that the Yama Kings only *believe* they can claim Asian souls, which then makes it true.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I honestly don't think those examples necessarily contradict what I pointed out. Mummies can still have however many soul &quot;parts&quot;, for the same reason vtm's 5 virtues(conscience, conviction, self control, instinct and courage) don't necessarily correspond to the high soul/low soul/willpower dictonomy. Each splat has their own quirks and special feature in Addition to what I've pointed out, I just mentioned the things that seemed more or less universal.<br /> <br /> As for spirits, I'd also like to point out the hsien also follow a yin/yang dictonomy with no &quot;Higher soul&quot; equivalent. I just say that there or probably many spirits out there that are genuinely different from the kind commonly encountered by garou, like the Awakened spirits encountered by mages in the high umbra or wraiths in the low umbra. Heck not all enemies in WTA core itself are necessarily related to the garou spirit world, a certain species of cephalopod/zombie virus critters from beneath the ocean comes to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 12-20-2019, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T18:42:14-08:00","id":1355315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1355283#post1355283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I honestly don't think those examples necessarily contradict what I pointed out. Mummies can still have however many soul &quot;parts&quot;, for the same reason vtm's 5 virtues(conscience, conviction, self control, instinct and courage) don't necessarily correspond to the high soul/low soul/willpower dictonomy. Each splat has their own quirks and special feature in Addition to what I've pointed out, I just mentioned the things that seemed more or less universal.<br /> <br /> As for spirits, I'd also like to point out the hsien also follow a yin/yang dictonomy with no &quot;Higher soul&quot; equivalent. I just say that there or probably many spirits out there that are genuinely different from the kind commonly encountered by garou, like the Awakened encountered by mages in the high umbra or wraiths in the low umbra. Heck not all enemies in WTA core itself are necessarily related to the garou spirit world, a certain species of cephalopod/zombie virus critters from beneath the ocean comes to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Chulorviah are shrouded in mystery but pretty solidly exist as extensions of a piece of the Wyrm, since they're primarily a Rokea antagonist and related to Qyrl-lings. While introduced in Blood-Dimmed Tides, none of the other games really seemed to do much with them, and they re-appeared in closer to W:tA format in the W20 Book of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T14:51:24-08:00","id":1356167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1355315#post1355315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Chulorviah are shrouded in mystery but pretty solidly exist as extensions of a piece of the Wyrm, since they're primarily a Rokea antagonist and related to Qyrl-lings. While introduced in Blood-Dimmed Tides, none of the other games really seemed to do much with them, and they re-appeared in closer to W:tA format in the W20 Book of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, cthulhu-virus people are wyrmish. Didn't know that. I thought they were aliens or something that didn't have any stakes in the triat Vs gaian war. Personally think that's kinda disappointing. <br /> <br /> I thought it was cool to have something not &quot;Wyrmish&quot; in the traditional sense to throw players for a loop. It's like something to remind us that while the Wyrm is the biggest threat to the world*(for the garou) right now, not everything is about the Wyrm. Some things are just weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T18:38:38-08:00","id":1356211,"title":"","content":"If you're using Werewolf as a base, everything falls into &quot;Wyld, Weaver or Wyrm&quot;. Even the weirdest shit is going to fall into some degree of chaos, order or entropy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T20:46:49-08:00","id":1356228,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but not everything needs to Work directly for the triat. Humans for instance are largely responsible for the weaver being able to do as much harm as it has, but they don't work for the weaver. They exist, they build technology or infrastructure to make their lives better, and the weaver is empowered as a result. The weaver's goals and humanities goals are entirely tangential to each other.<br /> <br /> It reminds me of a quote from the back of one of the WTA core books, &quot;If someone commits evil acts and builds up wyrm taint, that doesn't mean that they're working for the wyrm. Wyrm taint doesn't mean devil made them do it, it means that they did it and the devil noticed&quot;. It seems perfectly fine to me for the setting have weird creatures that don't directly fight the triatic conflict, because they could still serve to empower one side simply by existing.<br /> <br /> The Chulorviah could have been something that wasn't created by the triat for any reason, just a weird monster the spawned naturally from how the triat functions normally, and it could still be a problem because it's destructive and contagious swarm empowers the wyrm simply because it exists. It wouldn't need to fight for the wyrm or even know that the wyrm exists and it'd still be a problem that the garou would have to face because of it's very nature.<br /> <br /> I find things like that add variety to the setting, without the need for crossover shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T23:33:19-08:00","id":1356244,"title":"","content":"Reread section in W20 BotWyrm, and Chulorviah are in the oddball category with the Inquisitors rather than the definitely a Wyrm-originated monster section, but they also ping extremely strongly on Sense Wyrm, suggesting a much closer connection to corruption in spite of their apparent lack of care toward the Triat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T12:19:02-08:00","id":1356512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1355214#post1355214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or ghosts being given power from passions while dead, which is pretty heavily yin over yang.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually now that I think about it, all the supernaturals that fall on one side of the Life/Death split seem to need regular contact with the other side to survive.<br /> <br /> Vampires need the blood of the living, ghosts need passion, and mummies need to death cycle.<br /> <br /> Only one I'm not sure about is werewolves, unless one counts that they often need to leave the physical world, fall into deep meditation, or find spiritual holy places to rest in order to function as part of that yin-yang/death-life split.<br /> <br /> I could also see that as the other way though, the middle umbra is distinctly &quot;Living&quot; and they regain &quot;Living&quot; power from this exchange, but according to KotE vampires regain exclusively &quot;Yin/Death&quot; energy even though they replenish it with the energy of &quot;Life&quot; to make Vitae. Ghosts also hold exclusively &quot;Death/Yin&quot; energy according to both KotE and VTM's necromancy even though they feed of powerful emotions.<br /> <br /> I guess in order to get one you must feed it from a source of the Opposite? Changelings also need to replenish Glamour from mortals, the very Source of Banality....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 12-22-2019, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T13:17:58-08:00","id":1356522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1356512#post1356512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually now that I think about it, all the supernaturals that fall on one side of the Life/Death split seem to need regular contact with the other side to survive.<br /> <br /> Vampires need the blood of the living, ghosts need passion, and mummies need to death cycle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Passions are yin, though. This is something that a long time reading Weapons of the Gods has hammered into my recollections; anger, joy, obsessions, grief, fear... these are the things of the po, and facets of the yin outlook on life. Land of Eight Million Dreams also touches on this with what it terms &quot;Elemental Souls&quot;. Virtues are yang - what WotG referred to as Inspirations and what appear in Lo8MD as other facets of Elemental Souls. These are qualities like Benevolence (Wood), Faith (Water), or Righteousness (Metal).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only one I'm not sure about is werewolves, unless one counts that they often need to leave the physical world, fall into deep meditation, or find spiritual holy places to rest in order to function as part of that yin-yang/death-life split. </div> </div> </div>They require human and beast kin to persist - but undomesticated beasts are more important, as the existence of Mokole has it. They managed to persist for tens of millions of years without a Drachid form before shaping humans into being from early anthropoids (and subsequently, &quot;stealing&quot; the shape of humanity). In contrast, the sudden extinction of animal kin dooms one of the Changing Breeds to die in a single generation. Mokole can also hop across that barrier and get Bete to do the same, but that requires some forethought and prior action. It doesn't work after the kin are all dead.<br /> <br /> It's probably important to note that Garou and Fera aren't cursed into what they are, and that W:tA in general tends to flip whatever figurative tables of philosophy that humanity set up as a matter of course. Notions of what are complementary will not necessarily line up between Werewolf and human philosophies as a matter of course. Nagah live up to an ideal of Werewolf's balance, and Nagah could theoretically breed only among their own in perpetuity on account of how their special Nagah-Nagah-pairings only happen once in a mother's lifetime; at all other times, children are the mother's breed, even when their father is another serpent-changer. Kin, hence, tend to be practically necessary as an imbalance buffer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could also see that as the other way though, the middle umbra is distinctly &quot;Living&quot; and they regain &quot;Living&quot; power from this exchange, but according to KotE vampires regain exclusively &quot;Yin/Death&quot; energy even though they replenish it with the energy of &quot;Life&quot; to make Vitae. Ghosts also hold exclusively &quot;Death/Yin&quot; energy according to both KotE and VTM's necromancy even though they feed of powerful emotions. </div> </div> </div>Their passions feed their lower souls, and they associate these with death (NB: the po is the yin soul), and further, toward the demonic, as their bodily souls were sent through hell and reincarnated as preta. Virtues would bolster the non-demonic, non-hell parts of them, hence, so they would associated yang with life as such. This position is more or less their own, given their cursed rebirth status.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess in order to get one you must feed it from a source of the Opposite? Changelings also need to replenish Glamour from mortals, the very Source of Banality.... </div> </div> </div>Banality is kind of like the Wyrm - mortals just happen to act in a manner it &quot;likes&quot;, and which facilitates it. They can be argued as inviting it in, but it still exists, even without mortals to encourage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T16:58:45-08:00","id":1356553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1356522#post1356522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Passions are yin, though. This is something that a long time reading Weapons of the Gods has hammered into my recollections; anger, joy, obsessions, grief, fear... these are the things of the po, and facets of the yin outlook on life. Land of Eight Million Dreams also touches on this with what it terms &quot;Elemental Souls&quot;. Virtues are yang - what WotG referred to as Inspirations and what appear in Lo8MD as other facets of Elemental Souls. These are qualities like Benevolence (Wood), Faith (Water), or Righteousness (Metal).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that KotE Dharmabooks establish that the Higher/Lower soul dictonomy is neither yin nor yang. Some just see them as such. The Devil tigers in their book are said to believe the Po is heavily Yang aspected, to the point of calling it the &quot;Greater Yang Virtue&quot; and this is the Dharma that almost exclusively studies and practices with the Po.<br /> <br /> I myself don't believe the higher/lower soul + willpower split has anything to do with life-death/yang-yin dictonomy. At least they don't in World of Darkness specifically anyway, the Actual mythology may be different. In WOD Shen or Yi souls don't come into play and Hun doesn't represent a character's relationships to other people either for example. Honestly, I'd probably say it fits better with the triatic split mage and werewolf have, as all 3 aspects of order, chaos, and entropy can have both passive and active states.<br /> <br /> On another note, Weapons of the gods rpg probably isn't the best thing to compare to WOD. Both have entirely different views and philosophies when it comes to eastern mythology. Not to mention, EOS Press is also an american publisher like white-wolf, so they're likely to have taken their own creative liberties as american publishers are want to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1356522#post1356522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They require human and beast kin to persist - but undomesticated beasts are more important, as the existence of Mokole has it. They managed to persist for tens of millions of years without a Drachid form before shaping humans into being from early anthropoids (and subsequently, &quot;stealing&quot; the shape of humanity). In contrast, the sudden extinction of animal kin dooms one of the Changing Breeds to die in a single generation. Mokole can also hop across that barrier and get Bete to do the same, but that requires some forethought and prior action. It doesn't work after the kin are all dead.<br /> <br /> It's probably important to note that Garou and Fera aren't cursed into what they are, and that W:tA in general tends to flip whatever figurative tables of philosophy that humanity set up as a matter of course. Notions of what are complementary will not necessarily line up between Werewolf and human philosophies as a matter of course. Nagah live up to an ideal of Werewolf's balance, and Nagah could theoretically breed only among their own in perpetuity on account of how their special Nagah-Nagah-pairings only happen once in a mother's lifetime; at all other times, children are the mother's breed, even when their father is another serpent-changer. Kin, hence, tend to be practically necessary as an imbalance buffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't fera call the side effects of rage &quot;The Curse&quot; though? It drives away any human or animal without extraordinary willpower, throws them into mindless frenzies that hurt people close to them, and can put them into thrall of the Wyrm itself. As powerful a tool as rage is, it's as much a curse as any other supernatural has.<br /> <br /> I'm not exactly sure what Kin have to do with the &quot;creatures on one side of the Yin/Yang split need to embrace their opposite to replenish themselves&quot; thing I was talking about? You kinda lost me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1356522#post1356522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their passions feed their lower souls, and they associate these with death (NB: the po is the yin soul), and further, toward the demonic, as their bodily souls were sent through hell and reincarnated as preta. Virtues would bolster the non-demonic, non-hell parts of them, hence, so they would associated yang with life as such. This position is more or less their own, given their cursed rebirth status.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to point out &quot;yin&quot; of KotE and self control are &quot;virtues&quot; of yin, so I don't think the yin emotions and yang virtues thing holds. At least in WOD specifically, that a hsien Exclusive mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1356522#post1356522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banality is kind of like the Wyrm - mortals just happen to act in a manner it &quot;likes&quot;, and which facilitates it. They can be argued as inviting it in, but it still exists, even without mortals to encourage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banality is also kinda like the weaver and also kinda like the ebon dragon. Changelings also congregate around green pits of Balefire to restore glamour. I don't think the wyrm theory really fits.<br /> <br /> I also just finding it ironic the humans are the greatest source of both glamour and banality, 2 entirely opposite powers that effect changelings in opposite ways. Changeling also has a sort of balance them as well, banality may be the most obvious threat with how it's gotten out of control, but the dreaming's glamours are just as dangerous if left unchecked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 12-22-2019, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T17:47:02-08:00","id":1356561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1356553#post1356553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that KotE Dharmabooks establish that the Higher/Lower soul dictonomy is neither yin nor yang. Some just see them as such. The Devil tigers in their book are said to believe the Po is heavily Yang aspected, to the point of calling it the &quot;Greater Yang Virtue&quot; and this is the Dharma that almost exclusively studies and practices with the Po.<br /> <br /> I myself don't believe the higher/lower soul + willpower split has anything to do with life-death/yang-yin dictonomy. At least they don't in World of Darkness specifically anyway, the Actual mythology may be different. In WOD Shen or Yi souls don't come into play and Hun doesn't represent a character's relationships to other people either for example. Honestly, I'd probably say it fits better with the triatic split mage and werewolf have, as all 3 aspects of order, chaos, and entropy can have both passive and active states.</div> </div> </div> </div>In actual Daoism, the hun is yang and the po is yin. That's what I'm referring to. Land of Eight Million Dreams also goes along with this at least in part in its discussion of elemental souls, possibly because it had time to learn from KotE. Still not enough time to learn that &quot;hsien-xian&quot; doesn't work the way they think it does, though. Dragons of the East also got in on the side of &quot;po is yin, hun is yang&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note, Weapons of the gods rpg probably isn't the best thing to compare to WOD. Both have entirely different views and philosophies when it comes to eastern mythology. Not to mention, EOS Press is also an american publisher like white-wolf, so they're likely to have taken their own creative liberties as american publishers are want to do. </div> </div> </div>The difference is that WotG had actual Chinese cultural consultants on hand. While not an exhaustive guide dedicated to the subject, it's less removed from its sources, and seeks to demonstrate culture through stories, the context of which one gleans from taking in lore sheets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't fera call the side effects of rage &quot;The Curse&quot; though? It drives away any human or animal without extraordinary willpower, throws them into mindless frenzies that hurt people close to them, and can put them into thrall of the Wyrm itself. As powerful a tool as rage is, it's as much a curse as any other supernatural has. </div> </div> </div>It's still a poetic flourish above an actual thing. Heaven doesn't look down on the world and say, &quot;yeah, fuck that guy, he's going to turn into a wolf monster because we hate him and want to teach him a lesson.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not exactly sure what Kin have to do with the &quot;creatures on one side of the Yin/Yang split need to embrace their opposite to replenish themselves&quot; thing I was talking about? You kinda lost me. </div> </div> </div>It's the only real &quot;opposite&quot; component necessary for survival, in their case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like to point out &quot;yin&quot; of KotE and self control are &quot;virtues&quot; of yin, so I don't think the yin emotions and yang virtues thing holds. At least in WOD specifically, that a hsien Exclusive mechanic. </div> </div> </div>No, it's a reflection of something that isn't an attempt to hammer the concepts into Vampire Virtues in a rushed fashion. Were KotE to get revised, the present associations might well be the first things on the chopping block after the term &quot;Cathayan&quot;. The totally not hun and po for wraiths could go with them; if you're going to use the terms, it would be best to keep them at least slightly recognizable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Banality is also kinda like the weaver and also kinda like the ebon dragon. Changelings also congregate around green pits of Balefire to restore glamour. I don't think the wyrm theory really fits. </div> </div> </div>The Weaver's webs are an easy go in for the Defiler, the Wyrm's own shattered self-representation. It's rather ambiguous, but in any case, Banality is best treated more as a force unto itself than focused through the Triat, which is where the comparison with the Wyrm comes into play, as it's typically likened to the dark side of the force rather than a singular entity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also just finding it ironic the humans are the greatest source of both glamour and banality, 2 entirely opposite powers that effect changelings in opposite ways. Changeling also has a sort of balance them as well, banality may be the most obvious threat with how it's gotten out of control, but the dreaming's glamours are just as dangerous if left unchecked. </div> </div> </div>Gigantic mirths and terrible melancholies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T00:54:18-08:00","id":1356604,"title":"","content":"So I did some digging and the connection of Hun and P'o with Yang and Yin appears to be from around the 4-6th Centuries, BC. Before that, they were less well defined.<br /> <br /> Even then, the nature of them appears to be up for very different interpretations and, according to most, is a largely 'scholastic' or 'academic' endeavour, since the lay person rarely understands much difference between the two.<br /> <br /> When you read into their descriptions, there is a lot of overlap. Hun is Yang because it's 'bright', but technically it's also linked to the moon, which is 'dark' and hence Yin. The opposite also stands for the P'o.<br /> <br /> **ETA: It's P'o that's 'bright' and 'moon'. I'm getting them the wrong way around. The same point stands, though: they're mixed concepts.**<br /> <br /> I think that leaves enough scope for Kindred of the East's duality to work, but there's a simple enough explanation to reconcile the two:<br /> <br /> In mortals, the two 'souls' and the two Chi types are closely interwoven. The Hun is the seat of Yang but also contains many elements of Yin, and vice versa for the P'o, since these four concepts are largely interconnected and interdependent. <br /> <br /> The Gui-ren, on the other hand, as beings who have been torn apart in Hell and stitched back together by sheer willpower, represent an unnatural separation and dysregulation of what should be deeply unified components of the spirit.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, you could argue that it's the initial fracturing of the soul when the Gui-ren's P'o awakens in life that makes them easy targets for the Yama Kings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-24-2019, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T14:10:58-08:00","id":1356692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1356604#post1356604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I did some digging and the connection of Hun and P'o with Yang and Yin appears to be from around the 4-6th Centuries, BC. Before that, they were less well defined.<br /> <br /> Even then, the nature of them appears to be up for very different interpretations and, according to most, is a largely 'scholastic' or 'academic' endeavour, since the lay person rarely understands much difference between the two.<br /> <br /> When you read into their descriptions, there is a lot of overlap. Hun is Yang because it's 'bright', but technically it's also linked to the moon, which is 'dark' and hence Yin. The opposite also stands for the P'o.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source on hun being tied to the moon? Because the quoted sources on the wikipedia entry mentioned that po was bright and typically associated with the moon, whereas hun was dark and cloudy, but associated with the sky/heaven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that leaves enough scope for Kindred of the East's duality to work, but there's a simple enough explanation to reconcile the two:<br /> <br /> In mortals, the two 'souls' and the two Chi types are closely interwoven. The Hun is the seat of Yang but also contains many elements of Yin, and vice versa for the P'o, since these four concepts are largely interconnected and interdependent.<br /> <br /> The Gui-ren, on the other hand, as beings who have been torn apart in Hell and stitched back together by sheer willpower, represent an unnatural separation and dysregulation of what should be deeply unified components of the spirit.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, you could argue that it's the initial fracturing of the soul when the Gui-ren's P'o awakens in life that makes them easy targets for the Yama Kings. </div> </div> </div>I'd just assume cut it out, alongside the D&amp;D-sourced Tou Mu and demon archer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T19:22:29-08:00","id":1356739,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly not upset about the fact that KotE took artistic liberties with the mythology of the east, trying to stick to them now would require a massive overhaul of the system and tossing out large chunks of the lore made specifically for the setting. I say leave the majority and just tweak the parts that stuck out the worst.<br /> <br /> I also personally think that the current mess that is KotE better marries the wider WOD systems mechanically than a making the hun/po pull double duty as yin/yang would(at least as a measuring tool on how crossovers mix). I also like the game as is, so I'm biased.<br /> <br /> So I say let the KotE mythology be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T01:45:21-08:00","id":1356775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1356692#post1356692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Source on hun being tied to the moon? Because the quoted sources on the wikipedia entry mentioned that po was bright and typically associated with the moon, whereas hun was dark and cloudy, but associated with the sky/heaven.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd just assume cut it out, alongside the D&amp;D-sourced Tou Mu and demon archer.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. I got them the wrong way round. I'll go back and add a correction. (Side note: my brain fog is really bad at the moment.)<br /> <br /> P'o is 'bright' (yang) but 'moon' (yin). Same point, though: there's a mix of the two concepts. Likewise, in Daoism yang always contains a little bit of yin and vice versa. <br /> <br /> In humans that makes sense. In the Hungry Dead, who are more imbalanced, having them unnaturally twain makes sense, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Edits: Cognitive stuff a bit messed up right now. 12-24-2019, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T11:50:57-08:00","id":1356833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1353497-yama-kings-and-maeljin-incarna?p=1356739#post1356739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly not upset about the fact that KotE took artistic liberties with the mythology of the east, trying to stick to them now would require a massive overhaul of the system and tossing out large chunks of the lore made specifically for the setting. I say leave the majority and just tweak the parts that stuck out the worst.<br /> <br /> I also personally think that the current mess that is KotE better marries the wider WOD systems mechanically than a making the hun/po pull double duty as yin/yang would(at least as a measuring tool on how crossovers mix). I also like the game as is, so I'm biased.<br /> <br /> So I say let the KotE mythology be different.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's liberties, and then there's liberties taken 1:1 from Dungeons and Dragons. Having Tou Mu be Tou Mu from Deities and Demigods is way too self-indulgent and on the nose, and very derivative besides.<br /> <br /> As for the Hun and Po, you can mix up the Virtues again and have either of those have a new, different opposed Trait, so that they would be setting up slightly different teeter-totters that sum to the Trait max. You could borrow Torment from D:tF as the Hun's opposite and make it the rating for Demon Chi, and make Self-Control Yin's opposite. If they don't line up to other beings' ratings, that's fine; it was never KotE's aim nor its purpose nor necessity to try and glue everything together. It hardly matters, though; V5's setup pretty much torpedoes any chance of seeing this again. Blood Resonance would probably take the place of the Chi Virtues, and beyond that, the only difference would be giving their &quot;Beast&quot; its own Shadow Archetype and changing around the Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}